roy  this guy's out there twisting around  doing the jerk or twerking or whatever  else and then booming through the strike  right the middle blows it by a guy what  do you say to the baseball purists who  are like this isn't baseball it's like  whether you're a purist of the game or  if you like really enjoy what we do  we're all trying to grow the game for  the next generation looking around the  stands on a steamy tuesday night in  savannah with thousands clad and what  else banana costumes  it's working when you think of baseball  what do you normally think  i think of uh  you know like rules that you don't  really understand  no music no fun  ladies and gentlemen and how would you  describe this  party  party  entertainment the best show ever  viral moments be it the dancing umpire a  flaming bat  and both runners off on the pitch a  player on stilts or in a kilt happen all  night long  [Applause]  and don't forget the banana nana's  senior dance team what is your favorite  part about being a banana nana  the dancing just hearing the crowd roar  when we do specific moves the positivity  of everything that happens here in  banana land we swing in banana ball  you swing for the fences  always with everything  [Applause]  a big bet showing this bunch of bananas  has a lot of appeal  for cbs mornings i'm chris van glee  savannah  last month owner jessie cole announced  the savannah bananas intend to take  their show on the road starting in 2023  they will be playing banana ball all  over the country bananas balls rules  include a two hour time limit no walks  no bunting and foul balls cut by fans  can counting is outs how fun is that  it's all designed to make it more  efficient i just if i'm the visiting  team  how do you tolerate them you ain't  putting up with that well i don't know  or are you worn in advance like it's  going to get sillier i would think that  kind of storytelling is it reminds me of  why i love this show in the news  business because we get to tell stories  in anywhere america that are fun you  should take your kids to something like  that yeah they love that it is it's  chris appealing the players actually do  not get paid but the team has more  social media followers than any major  league baseball team make money off that  yeah
 

